Cutting a command-window range straddling cmdpt clamps cmdpt to p1 (raspdelete 113).
After "1p" executes, cmdpt=25; typing unexecuted text past it then cutting across
the boundary exercises the p2>cmdpt branch.

-- input --
hello world
-- proto --
Hversion 2
Hnewname tag=0
Hmovname tag=0 "input"
Tversion 2
Tstartcmdfile
Hnewname tag=1
Hbindname tag=1
Hcurrent tag=1
Hmovname tag=1 "~~sam~~"
Hcheck0 tag=1
Hack
Tack
Hunlock
Tstartfile 0
Hbindname tag=0
Hcurrent tag=0
Hgrow tag=0 p=0 n=12
Hcheck0 tag=0
Hcheck0 tag=0
Hack
Trequest 0 0 12
Hdata tag=0 p=0 "hello world\n"
Tack
Hgrow tag=1 p=0 n=10
Hcheck0 tag=1
Hack
Trequest 1 0 10
Hdata tag=1 p=0 " +. input\n"
Tack
Hsetdot tag=1 p=10 n=10
Hunlock
cmd 1p\n
Hgrowdata tag=1 p=13 n=12 "hello world\n"
Hcheck0 tag=1
Hack
Tack
Hsetdot tag=1 p=25 n=25
Hsetdot tag=0 p=0 n=12
Hunlock
Ttype 1 25 xyz
Tcut 1 24 27
Texit
